---
title: Easy Flatbread No Yeast
servings: 6
cuisine: mediterranean
main_protein: none
prep_time: "20 minutes"
cook_time: "10 minutes"
tags:
  - dinner
  - flour
  - flatbread
  - bread
source: https://www.inspiredtaste.net/46128/no-yeast-flatbread/
image: ../obsidian/attachments/No-Yeast-Flatbread.jpg
leftover_portions: 2
prep:
  - Whisk together flour, baking powder and salt
  - Measure 0.75 cup cold water
  - Flour a work surface
---
Mix dry ingredients: Whisk together @all-purpose flour{2%cups}, @baking powder{1.5%tsp}, and @fine sea salt{1%tsp} in a large bowl.

Create dough: Make a well in the center, add @olive oil{2%tbsp}, @maple syrup{1%tsp} (or sugar), and most of the @cold water{0.75%cup}. Stir with a #rubber spatula{} until combined, adding remaining water if needed.

Knead and rest: Transfer to floured surface and knead 5-10 times until smooth. Cover and rest ~{10%minutes}.

Roll out: Divide dough into six pieces. Dust with flour and roll each into a disc ⅛-¼ inch thick.

Cook: Heat 1-2 tablespoons @avocado oil{} in a #skillet{} over medium heat. Cook flatbreads until golden (~{1%minute} per side).

Keep warm: Transfer to a plate, cover with towel to retain warmth.

-- Flour: 2 cups is about 260 g; water: 0.75 cup is about 175 ml.
